  "sourceFindings": [
    "Four separate pale/vitreous triangular-crescent pockets lie around the four central glass petals, between their continuous darkcame and the outer circular frame. They are distinct from the centralfourpetals and from the three largeupperlobes.",
    "Native confirms the small upperrosette/came context, but fine pocket boundaries are subtexel at64x256; actual prepared512RGB supplies measured contacts. No symmetry/mirror shortcut used: four finitepolygon traces reflect small actual asymmetries.",
    "The four glass witnesses were unmasked in v1. Proposed four-pocket support includes each; adjacent continuousbrown/black came witnesses remain excluded.",
    "Painted warm/dark pixels inside visible pocketglass remain glass; brown metal/came stays structural. This is visual sourceclassification, not a globalRGBthreshold or brightness-derived architecture."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Finite manually traced boundaries approximate actual antialiased contact within about1masterpixel; cyanoverlay and originalRGB must be independently reviewed, not treated as exact recovered sourcegeometry.",
    "No scalar planes, amplitude, smoothing or height data authored or accepted here. Thin pocket geometry and existingbevel interaction still require integrated source/physical review.",
